  "name": "Example: Equating Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Number to Solve For an Unknown Quantity",
  "problem": "Given that $3+2\\textrm{i} = a + \\textrm{i}b,$ calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n3 = a\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n2 = b\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3$ and $b=2.$",
